# Gemma 4 E4B instruct (google/gemma-4-E4B-it; 4B effective parameters, 8B with the per-layer
# embeddings; Apache-2.0), official bf16 checkpoint: the Gemma 4B-class point of the speed/quality
# study (reports/speed_quality/). Its template thinks only when asked (enable_thinking defaults to
# false; set explicitly here) and injects no system turn; the prefill renders as
# `<|turn>model\nAnswer:`. --enforce-eager: with torch.compile the profiling run tried to
# allocate a second 5.25 GiB copy of the per-layer embedding table (262,144 x 10,752 bf16; inductor
# appears to fold its scale into the weight [INFERENCE]) and ran out of memory; eager mode loads and serves. The
# workload is prefill only (one generated token per request), which CUDA graphs barely touch.
# --language-model-only skips the vision and audio towers; --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 and
# --max-num-seqs=16 as in the other presets; --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling
# defaults; 0.90 of the GPU.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=google/gemma-4-E4B-it
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=ee0ef6023621cff504d758262d4e04895a5af4a2
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.90
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking":false}'
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --enforce-eager --max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 --generation-config=vllm'
